---
id: org.dxos.plugin.illustrator
name: IllustratorPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A headless diagramming host plugin for `DXOS` Composer. Owns the base `Sketch` ECHO type, the
renderer-neutral scene DSL and dialect registry, and the agent-facing sketch skill/operations.
Canvas renderers (e.g. plugin-tldraw, plugin-excalidraw) contribute a `SketchVariant` capability
supplying their canvas schema, a builder that maps the scene DSL onto their records, and surface
components; plugin-illustrator resolves the variant at runtime and delegates.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`        |

## Types

```mdl
type Sketch
  desc: Named handle around a renderer-specific canvas object.
  fields:
    name?: string
    canvas: Ref<Unknown>   # reference to the renderer-specific canvas (e.g. Tldraw.Canvas)
```

## Capabilities

```mdl
component VariantProvider
  desc: Contributed by renderer plugins; supplies the canvas type, a scene-DSL builder
        (read/apply), a create factory, and Article/Card surface components.
```

## Operations

```mdl
op create
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.create
  desc: Creates a Sketch with an empty canvas for the requested (or default) variant.

op read
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.read
  desc: Returns the current scene of a sketch as world objects with object-local coordinates.

op edit
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.edit
  desc: Applies scene commands to a sketch via the variant's builder; returns the resulting scene.

op generate
  key: org.dxos.operation.illustrator.generate
  desc: Replaces a sketch with a diagram compiled from mermaid source (flowchart or classDiagram);
        the dialect owns the layout, so no coordinates are supplied.
```

## Dialects

Higher-level diagram languages compile to scene commands (see `src/model/dialect.ts`); each
dialect owns its layout, so its output lands as ordinary world objects that stay editable by id.

```mdl
component MermaidFlowchart
  desc: Mermaid flowchart subset (nodes, subgraphs, directed edges) with a layered layout.

component UmlClass
  desc: Mermaid classDiagram subset (class blocks with members, stereotypes, generics, and the
        standard relation arrows) with a layered layout — supertypes above subtypes. Each class
        compiles to a world object with title/attributes/methods compartments.

component UmlGrid
  desc: Grid variant — equal-size cells on the document grid (GRID=32), barycenter column
        alignment, orthogonal Z-routed connectors.

component UmlEngine
  desc: Engine-backed placement (dagre | ELK layered) over the grid cells and routing — proper
        crossing minimization and straightness; see docs/DESIGN.md.
```

## Variants

```mdl
component SvgVariant
  desc: SVG renderer variant owned by this plugin (peer of tldraw/excalidraw): the scene DSL is
        stored verbatim as canvas records (SvgHandler/SvgBuilder) and rendered read-only via
        SceneSvg.
```

## Skills

```mdl
component DrawingSkill
  desc: Free-form drawing via the scene DSL; the agent does the layout.

component UmlSkill
  desc: UML class diagrams from source code (bound documents or a fetched GitHub reference):
        the agent extracts the class model, emits a mermaid classDiagram, and the generate
        operation compiles and lays it out.
```

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Create, edit, and read back a drawing
  desc: |
    The scene-DSL round-trip through the SVG variant (owned by this plugin, so no renderer plugin
    dependency is needed). Note: the source's runtime ECHO type is `Drawing`, not the `Sketch`
    type documented above — this flow uses the real name.
  actors: agent
  covers: []
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - no drawing named "QA Sketch" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create the drawing
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Drawing (or ask the assistant to create one). Name it "QA Sketch".
      invoke: [op:create] { name: "QA Sketch", variant: "svg" }
      capture: created
      expect: a Drawing named "QA Sketch" exists with an empty SVG canvas
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (no separate gesture — the navtree create action places it for you)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "QA Sketch" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Edit the scene
      do: Ask the assistant to draw a rectangle labeled "Start" at the origin.
      invoke: [op:edit] { drawing: $created.object, commands: [{ _tag: "upsert", id: "start", shape: { _tag: "rect", label: "Start", x: 0, y: 0, width: 120, height: 60 } }] }
      capture: edited
      expect: a rectangle labeled "Start" renders on the canvas
      assert: return $edited.upserted.includes('start')
    - name: Read the scene back
      do: (no separate gesture — the canvas already shows the result of the edit)
      invoke: [op:read] { drawing: $created.object }
      expect: the returned scene's world objects include the "start" shape with the coordinates just written
      assert: return $result.scene.objects?.some((o) => o.id === 'start')
  after:
    - name: Delete the drawing
      do: Right-click "QA Sketch" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

```mdl
flow QA-2: Generate a UML class diagram from mermaid source
  desc: The UmlSkill path — replace a drawing's contents with a class diagram compiled from mermaid source, with layout owned by the dialect.
  actors: agent
  covers: []
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - no drawing named "QA UML" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Create the drawing
      do: Ask the assistant to create a new drawing named "QA UML".
      invoke: [op:create] { name: "QA UML", variant: "svg" }
      capture: created
      expect: an empty Drawing named "QA UML" exists
      assert: return !!$created.object
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (no separate gesture)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.collection }
      expect: "QA UML" appears as a row under the collection
    - name: Generate from a mermaid classDiagram
      do: |
        Ask the assistant to render this class diagram into "QA UML":
        classDiagram
          class Animal { +String name +makeSound() }
          class Dog
          Animal <|-- Dog
      invoke: |
        [op:generate] { drawing: $created.object, source: "classDiagram\n  class Animal { +String name +makeSound() }\n  class Dog\n  Animal <|-- Dog\n" }
      expect: two class boxes ("Animal", "Dog") render with a supertype-above-subtype layered layout and an inheritance arrow between them, replacing the drawing's prior contents
      assert: return $result.upserted.length >= 2
  after:
    - name: Delete the drawing
      do: Right-click "QA UML" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```
